<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "EC number is a unique identification number assigned to a chemical substance in the European Union. It is used to identify substances in regulatory databases, safety data sheets (SDSs), and chemical legislation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The EC number is a seven-digit identifier typically written in the format XXX-XXX-X and used to identify chemical substances in European regulatory inventories.\n\nExample:\nSubstance: Ethanol\nEC number: 200-578-6"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#EC> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EC"@en .
