# https://w3id.org/eudpp#batch
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#batch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#batch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductIdentifierGranularity> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#batch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘batch’ usually refers to a subset of a specific model composed of all products produced in a specific manufacturing plant at a specific moment in time (ESPR preamble (33))."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#batch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "batch"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#item
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#item> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#item> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductIdentifierGranularity> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#item> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘item’ usually refers to a single unit of a model (ESPR preamble (33))."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#item> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "item"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/eudpp#model
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#model> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#model> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#ProductIdentifierGranularity> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "According to ESPR Art 9 (2d) the digital product passport is to be established at model, batch or item level, and the definition of such levels is given by delegated acts;\n\nThe term ‘model’ usually refers to a version of a product of which all units share the same technical characteristics relevant for the ecodesign requirements and the same model identifier (ESPR preamble (33))."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp#model> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "model"@en .
